WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.230
What does true evil look like?

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.670
It's a question that many screenplays and
Anime have failed to answer over the years.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.690
And Mahito, is one of the best answers I have
come across in a long while.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.220
And in this video I will explain to you exactly
why.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.780
Why this handsome little Frankenstein here,
is one of the most eerie, repulsive and horrifying

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.520
villains in all of Anime.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.700
A villain that clearly has been carefully
crafted with a clever mix of human psychology

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:37.340
and Gege Akutami's ingenious storytelling
abilities, to creep the hell out of you and

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.820
make you loath him with every pore of your
body.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.930
A core piece of what makes the story of Jujutsu
Kaisen so fantastic.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:57.280
That - aaand what's the deal the with all
the hands.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:07.479
This is the story of the most horrible and
human curse of them all, Mahito.

00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:22.940
With Sukuna, I have already discussed one
of the three major villains of Jujutsu Kaisen,

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:28.400
and yet, just like Geto, Mahito is a completely
different trope of antagonist.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.619
All three of them represent fundamentally
different versions of evil, which makes the

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:40.900
story so much more interesting and versatile.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.280
And yet, out of all three, Mahito is the only
one that Akutami has created with the intent

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.500
to portray true evil.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.080
The most dangerous and vile cursed spirit
in the story right now, and I would even go

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.800
as far as to say overall.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.390
But as you probably have figured out already,
Mahito's horror lies not within how powerful

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.630
he is, but in his personality.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.820
Don't you think it's interesting that he is
the only curse that takes the form of a human

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:06.820
in the story?

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:17.840
Mahito is all soul this and hands that, oh,
and he has the same blue eyes that Gojo has.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.230
The genius of Mahito's character, that will
be crystal clear if you make it to the end

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:27.280
of this video, is completely based on the
unique role he takes in the Jujutsu world.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:33.340
Despite being teased to us as one of the most
scary curses, what stands out most about Mahito

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:37.130
is actually his extremely human appearance.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.900
The Frankenstein-esk appearance paired with
a quite extroverted and curious personality,

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:49.270
as well as a soft and kind voice that lets
every hair on my neck stand on end, at first

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:54.110
glance make him hard to differentiate from
the equal quirky looking Jujutsu students.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.700
In fact, it takes quite a while before we
even get a sense that this is actually the

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.239
most purely evil character out of all in this
story.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:08.980
Especially his early relationship with the
harshly bullied Junpei creates the illusion

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.930
that this might be an exceptionally nice curse.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:18.269
Well, you know how that turned out in the
end.

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:26.930
- Mahito serves as the embodiment of human
selfishness, cruelty and desire.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:32.540
If you pay close attention, you will see that
all of his terrible traits and flaws are perfectly

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.110
human ones.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.110
Human pettiness.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.210
Human jealousy.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.280
Human fickleness.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:42.030
Mahito represents all the bad that humans
do to themselves and to others.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.430
The worst of us.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:56.489
What Akutami has done here is masterfully
embody the moral theme of his story this character.

00:03:56.489 --> 00:03:58.080
Curses vs. humans.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:05.019
Because, just like Yuji is both human and
curse, Mahito is also both curse and human.

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:07.940
And this parallel is no accident.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:14.950
In general, as the main antagonist of the
major first part of the story, Mahito's most

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.949
obvious role in is being a foil to the protagonist.

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:24.229
As so often is the case, these two characters
mirror each other in many ways and find themself

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.839
inextricably drawn to each other.

00:04:26.839 --> 00:04:30.600
Both Itadori and Mahito are newcomers to the
Jujutsu game.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:35.139
Itadori was just a regular high school student
until the other day, while Mahito has only

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:39.300
quite recently been awakened.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:45.869
Now, this is just me speculating, but I would
bet my left ball that that someone had their

00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:54.099
hands in creating Mahito, the guy LITERALLY
IS STITCHED TOGETHER, but we'll have to wait

00:04:54.099 --> 00:04:55.099
and see.

00:04:55.099 --> 00:05:00.509
Nonetheless, both of them are extremely powerful
and have very polarizing views of the world.

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:14.770
As becomes clear in their first encounter
under Nanami, both of them are basically children.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.770
They both want to get stronger, test their
abilities and have their influence on the

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:22.409
world, while responsibly thinking through
their actions and motivations.

00:05:22.409 --> 00:05:27.719
Just kidding, they're of course both crazily
impulse-driven and keep dramatically underestimating

00:05:27.719 --> 00:05:28.900
those around them.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.270
Both Itadori and Mahito live in their own
little world, where they are the hunters,

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.400
the Gojo's who force their will on the world.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.649
Yuji trying to save anyone and anything that
moves.

00:05:41.649 --> 00:05:47.729
And Mahito literally going full reptile brain,
basically only following every impulse he

00:05:47.729 --> 00:05:48.860
ever has.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.860
Food.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.860
Kill.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:51.860
Play.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:52.860
BLurrrb....

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:58.029
Mahito with a child's curiosity is testing
his own powers, learning about the world and

00:05:58.029 --> 00:06:07.509
even spending time with humans to transfigure
out of they work.

00:06:07.509 --> 00:06:08.509
-

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:13.050
The funny thing is, that Mahito's biggest
desire is proving to himself and to everyone

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:19.729
that he is the purest curse, the king of courses
if you will.

00:06:19.729 --> 00:06:22.360
- Sorry.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:27.830
He tries to convince Junpei to live more like
a curse, and yet the big irony here, is that

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.809
Mahito actually doesn't get how curses REALLY
are.

00:06:32.809 --> 00:06:38.309
Take the other intelligent curses with him:
Jogo, Nanami and baby Cuthulu.

00:06:38.309 --> 00:06:43.179
These guys are probably ancient, born from
peoples fear of nature.

00:06:43.179 --> 00:06:45.189
They behave quite differently from Mahito.

00:06:45.189 --> 00:06:51.259
Yes, they are all somewhat murderous and hateful
towards humans and they all seem to be dominated

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:56.719
by their impulses, BUT they also: plan ahead,
they have a higher purpose that they are willing

00:06:56.719 --> 00:07:03.389
to die for and they even care about their
comrades.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:12.020
- hell, let's be real, Hanami is probably
nicer than half of the jujutsu sorcerers themselves.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:17.149
Mahito on the other hand, is like a textbook
sociopath, he does everything impulsively,

00:07:17.149 --> 00:07:21.289
he manipulates those around him for his own
sake, when things get tough he decides to

00:07:21.289 --> 00:07:27.389
run and afterwards is smug about it, and he
doesn't really care about the other curses

00:07:27.389 --> 00:07:29.979
around him.

00:07:29.979 --> 00:07:39.539
Now, I'm gonna drop a big bombshell on you
here, and if you didn't know this you'll have

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:40.830
to subscribe.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:45.800
Jujutsu Kaisen is not only heavily inspired
by other SHounen like Bleach or Hunter x Hunter,

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:52.489
it is also filled to the brim with the psychological
concepts of Freud and Jung, who both are considered

00:07:52.489 --> 00:07:55.349
the founders of modern psychoanalysis.

00:07:55.349 --> 00:08:00.719
While both men had different models of the
human mind, both of them had the theme of

00:08:00.719 --> 00:08:07.110
the Id, the ego or the shadow, that basically
describes the unconscious part of your personality,

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:12.319
that you are unaware of, but that drives your
basic needs, desires and instincts, compared

00:08:12.319 --> 00:08:30.499
to our active conscious mind.

00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:34.509
It's something that nowadays you might call
the feeling and the thinking brain.

00:08:34.509 --> 00:08:39.459
And while we all love to think that we make
rational decisions all the time, guess what:

00:08:39.459 --> 00:08:41.899
The feeling brain is in command.

00:08:41.899 --> 00:08:46.709
As the psychologist Jonathan Heidth put it,
we are basically the elephant and its rider.

00:08:46.709 --> 00:08:51.399
We can consciously try to steer our feeling
brain in the direction we want to go, but

00:08:51.399 --> 00:08:56.410
if the elephant reaaaally wants to do something,
it'll do it and there's nothing you can do

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:57.509
about it.

00:08:57.509 --> 00:09:00.880
Mahito is the embodiment of exactly that.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.750
He is pure feeling brain.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.949
Pure instinct.

00:09:03.949 --> 00:09:05.190
Pure pleasure.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.190
Pure doing what feels good in the moment.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.880
He is only that.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:20.300
No emotions and no rational, something that
even the other curses have to some extend.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:28.310
And that's what makes Mahito so absolutely
terrifying.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:31.000
Why he creeps you the f''k out.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:37.139
Mahito is a mirror for us humans in which
we see our rawest and darkest instincts reflected

00:09:37.139 --> 00:09:38.440
back at us.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:44.800
Mahito is the essence of human evil and human
darkness compiled into a character.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:51.980
And the reason why Itadori hates him so much,
is exactly because of that.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:59.149
He sees himself reflected in Mahito.

00:09:59.149 --> 00:10:01.459
All the stuff that he feels insecure about.

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:03.250
His values and ideals.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:08.410
Itadori's big thing is saving people and under
no circumstances hurt them.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:13.550
And yet, Mahito not only plays with the life
of his own comrades, but he also forces Yuji

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:19.680
to kill himself and break his rules.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:26.470
But I think the true reason lies even a bit
deeper.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:39.399
Consider this scene here, where Gojo asses
Yuji's personality: - Yuji wants to save everyone

00:10:39.399 --> 00:10:45.810
and condemns killing, but he has no problem,
right from the start to absolutely decimate

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:49.220
curses, even though they still take the form
of living creatures.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.550
To him, curses are all the same.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:55.930
Their existence doesn't have any worth in
itself, and he doesn't flinch to terminate

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.329
them if needed.

00:10:57.329 --> 00:11:00.050
Does that sound familiar?

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:04.629
- Mahito shows Yuji that they are pretty much
the same, just on opposite sites.

00:11:04.629 --> 00:11:09.339
And the fact that the lines between curses
and humans keep blurring more and more as

00:11:09.339 --> 00:11:13.279
the story continues just places more contrast
on this.

00:11:13.279 --> 00:11:19.040
Mahito in a very interesting way, slowly but
steadily forces Yuji to deal with his own

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:24.100
insecurities, his own values and his own hypocrisy
as a person.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:29.610
It's not good enough to think that every human
life is valuable, he now has to find an answer

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.100
as to why.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:36.430
We can see this clash of their ideals in how
both of them try to push Junpei to act in

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:54.550
the sense of their respective values.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:12:00.300
But there is even more humanity in Mahito,
that makes his horror and evil seem even greater

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:01.740
than it already is.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:09.360
If I were to ask you why x random psycho monster
in y scary movie is evil, you might say something

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:13.089
like: Well he is evil, cause he doesn't have
a heart or a soul.

00:12:13.089 --> 00:12:14.889
So what does Akutami do?

00:12:14.889 --> 00:12:20.990
Make Mahito all about that.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:31.050
Mahito 
can literally see and manipulate souls, the

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.040
essence of everything.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:37.940
And so for him, the soul is nothing special,
but just something else that is just there.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:43.940
No difference between a plant and an ant and
a human, except for human reasoning, which

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:49.230
Mahito explicitly detests.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:54.079
He transforms and plays with people's souls
to try out his powers.

00:12:54.079 --> 00:12:57.529
Using people's souls and their deaths to break
Yuji?

00:12:57.529 --> 00:12:58.720
Exhilarating.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:03.650
The harrowing fact that Mahito is playing
with the most valuable thing a human has,

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:12.500
their soul, which at least in the Jujutsu
world is a real thing, is Wonderfully represented

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:20.809
by the concept of hands.

00:13:20.809 --> 00:13:28.470
- Mahito has the power to touch the essence
of who you are.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.990
His hands are literally the touch of death.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.370
And that's also what makes Mahito so brilliant
as a piece of writing.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.360
He represents you as a human, but also death
itself.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:42.160
It's all torment, violence and cruelty.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:47.430
Notice how people keep reflecting on their
ideas about and relationship towards death

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.449
whenever they come into contact with Mahito.

00:13:50.449 --> 00:13:53.140
- Nanami, Junpei, Itadori.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:58.449
Looking at Mahito not only mirrors human life,
it also mirrors human death.

00:13:58.449 --> 00:14:00.540
The essence of human experience.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:06.639
And that is an absolutely terrifying thing
to do, contemplating our own mortality and

00:14:06.639 --> 00:14:07.639
faultiness.

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:13.270
Which exactly why Mahito, in my eyes, is absolutely
perfectly written evil.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:18.139
Something that as Akutami mentioned in an
interview, he was absolutely going for.

00:14:18.139 --> 00:14:20.930
So: Is Mahito all evil then?

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:24.149
No character arc, except growing stronger
and more cruel?

00:14:24.149 --> 00:14:27.430
I would say no.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:32.449
Mahito's answer the central moral question
of the story, what does it mean to live a

00:14:32.449 --> 00:14:40.070
life worth living is simple: Life is worthless,
so I should enjoy myself and follow my instincts.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:43.529
Now, can we actually say that this is wrong.

00:14:43.529 --> 00:14:46.019
I think we can.

00:14:46.019 --> 00:14:51.000
The answer that Akutami is going for, for
all his characters, is that a good life worth

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:59.740
living always includes forming relationships
and bonds with others.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:09.079
You can even see the curses doing it, in their
small little curse family, where they care

00:15:09.079 --> 00:15:10.079
for each other.

00:15:10.079 --> 00:15:16.259
In short: The moral of JuJutsu Kaisen is that
true happiness and purpose comes from acting

00:15:16.259 --> 00:15:18.709
compassionate towards others.

00:15:18.709 --> 00:15:20.509
That's why Mahito is wrong.

00:15:20.509 --> 00:15:25.660
And the fact that he tries so hard to be the
perfect curse, just underlines how human he

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:26.660
is.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:29.490
This irony is actually wonderfully represented
by his name.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:32.540
Do you know what Mahito literally means?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:33.779
True human.

00:15:33.779 --> 00:15:34.779
Yeah.

00:15:34.779 --> 00:15:40.579
Ironic - Mahito is on a journey to figure
out the essence of his own soul, who he really

00:15:40.579 --> 00:15:41.579
is.

00:15:41.579 --> 00:15:46.499
And at some point, he might have to face the
fact that he is actually more human than curse.

00:15:46.499 --> 00:15:51.369
And I really hope we get to see more of that,
as I think he is the perfect antagonist for

00:15:51.369 --> 00:15:53.120
Yuji in the story.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:58.290
Sukuna is absolutely fantastic, but he is
way to complex and cool in my opinion to have

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:11.579
the same sense of evil and horror that Mahito
spreads on such a fundamental level.

00:16:11.579 --> 00:16:12.579
-

00:16:12.579 --> 00:16:15.680
Now for the bonus pay off of this video.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:26.339
Why does Mahito also have this beautiful blue
eye that reminds us so much of Gojo?

00:16:26.339 --> 00:16:30.600
I think this is done quite on purpose, as
the two of them share some quite interesting

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.600
traits.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:36.899
Their body language, especially their eyes
radiate absolute certainty of their superiority.

00:16:36.899 --> 00:16:40.819
They might appear childish and frivolous on
the surface, but if you plunge their depths

00:16:40.819 --> 00:16:45.850
they have a deeper understanding of themselves
and their desires than most other characters

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:46.850
in the series.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:50.649
They might not get other people, but that’s
not their priority either.

00:16:50.649 --> 00:16:54.079
And as we know, the eyes are the gates to
the soul.

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:58.860
What makes both of them so special, is that
both Mahito and Gojo can see things others

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:05.180
can't.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:10.110
Gojo's six eyes allow him to perceive everything
about a person, while Mahito is capable of

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.120
seeing the soul itself.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:17.010
This results in both of them seeing everything
which results in both of them being unable

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.569
to see people as individuals.

00:17:19.569 --> 00:17:23.919
- And that's why Mahito has the same blue
eye as Gojo.

00:17:23.919 --> 00:17:27.510
As we all know though, what is much more important
than your soul.

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.649
Is having a well defined six pack.

00:17:29.649 --> 00:17:44.130
Which is why the next video is about - my
feast friend -

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:47.270
Make sure to watch Todo's video here.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.620
Thanks for watching.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.530
Peace.

